# ⚠️⚠️ The harvest runs on a Linux runner and this repo is edited on Windows.
# A `.sh` checked out with CRLF fails as `/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter`, and a
# CRLF `run:` block in a workflow hands every line to bash with a trailing
# carriage return. Git already stores LF here, so nothing is wrong today — this
# is so that a future `core.autocrlf` setting on somebody's machine cannot make
# it wrong in a way that only shows up in CI.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
